/* The push copy (decision 0067).

   APNs resolves `loc-key` / `loc-args` against this table, so the server sends
   a key and LOOP owns every visible word. Nothing here names an amount, an
   address, a ticker, a balance, a code, a message body or a community — a
   notification says what kind of thing happened and where to look, and the app
   re-reads the authoritative state after the tap (03 §15.1).

   The table is deliberately not localized into an `.lproj` folder: LOOP ships
   one language, and a bundle-root table is the one iOS falls back to for every
   region rather than only for the one that was built. */

